      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ce09c4ff1ef661188867ab5|full_name}: No, Simulation time isn't accurate enough unfortunately and as Owl said is affected by other factors.\n\nThe idea here is simply to readily allow Karaoke world creators to start the music video for each individual player in a way that takes into account the voice latency of the person who queued the song to the player in question, so that each player hears the person who queued the song roughly in sync with the video that's playing regardless of latency differences.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
